        "result": "Built EXACT Z[zeta_7] arithmetic for the coset kernel and proved three structural facts, but the one that would bound the sum does not transfer to the integer lattice. (1) FACTORIZATION re-verified exactly: K(n) = [prod_j 1/(2*pi*i*n_j)] * D7(n mod 7), arch part REAL (i^6=-1), match 1e-9. (2) GALOIS-EQUIVARIANCE (exact): D7(a*c) = sigma_a(D7(c)) for all a in F_7^* (sigma_a: zeta->zeta^a). (3) FIELD-TRACE COLLAPSE (exact): the dilation-orbit sum Sum_{a in F_7^*} D7(a*c) = Tr_{Q(zeta_7)/Q}(D7(c)) is an INTEGER -- the cyclotomic oscillation rationalizes after averaging over the full multiplicative group (the Euler/QR even-factor cancellation). Tr(D7(1,1,1,1,1,1))=7!=5040, max|Tr|=9240=2^3*3*5*7*11, Sum of Tr over all orbit reps = 0, and it vanishes on EACH #QR-pattern class independently. (4) REALITY: since 6 = -1 mod 7 is a NON-residue, D7(-c)=D7(6c)=sigma_6(D7(c))=conj(D7(c)), so the n<->-n lattice pairing cancels every imaginary part EXACTLY -- the correction is RIGOROUSLY REAL. THE GAP: the trace collapse requires the F_7^* dilation c->a*c, which is NOT a lattice symmetry (it permutes residues mod 7 with no integer-lattice counterpart). Direct measurement: within a dilation orbit the lattice weights W_{ac} differ by mean spread 0.37-1.2 (not ~0), so Sum_c W_c D7(c) does NOT regroup into Sum_orbits W*Tr(D7). D7 is also generically NOT in Q(sqrt(-7)) (only 7/404 cosets fixed by sigma_2), so the QR/NQR index-2 split alone does not diagonalize -- the collapse needs the full F_7^* trace, which the lattice breaks. So the QR/Gauss angle delivers the exact REALITY reduction but NOT a magnitude/convergence bound for wide E.",
        "evidence": "All claims verified by exact computation. Files at C:\\Users\\Eliott\\Documents\\GitHub\\math\\04-computation\\: lrc14_qr_factorization_check_kps.py (K=arch*D7 to 1e-9, 5 cases incl wide), lrc14_qr_coset_structure_kps.py (full 46656-coset numeric scan: Sum_c D7=0 on every #QR class, mean|D7| symmetric under #QR<->6-#QR, Gauss sum g=i*sqrt7 verified g^2=-7), lrc14_qr_symmetry_mechanism_kps.py (exact Z[zeta_7]: D7(a*c)=sigma_a(D7(c)) all tested; dilation-orbit-sum coeffs=[5040,0,0,0,0,0] etc = rational trace; only 7/404 sampled D7 in Q(sqrt-7)), lrc14_qr_trace_bound_kps.py (7776 orbit reps: max|Tr|=9240, Sum Tr=0, vanishes per #QR class), lrc14_qr_lattice_apply_kps.py (DECISIVE: on AP8/WIDE8 lattices L=4,6 correction Im/Re~1e-15 so REAL confirmed; within-orbit weight spread 0.37-1.2 so trace collapse does NOT apply to lattice). Logged as HYP-2657 in 05-knowledge/hypotheses/INDEX.md.",
        "next_step": "The reality reduction is now exact and rigorous; fold it into the live route. Since the correction = Sum_c W_c * Re(D7(c)) with W_c real and |Re D7| <= 0.1431 (HYP-2646), the open analytic content is now purely the SIGNED real lattice weights W_c = Sum_{n=c mod 7} w(n). Two concrete follow-ups: (a) test whether Re(D7(c)), grouped by dilation orbit, has a sign pattern matching the sign of the dominant W_c so that orbit-wise partial sums are sign-definite (would give an absolute bound despite unequal weights); (b) since the far-element plateau route (HYP-2655/HYP-2653, the uniform decorrelation constant C(k)) is the live crux and is itself a 1-D breakpoint discrepancy weighted by missed-sector phase s/7, re-express that discrepancy through Re(D7) and check whether the trace integrality bounds the resonant (w shares factors with e's) breakpoint contributions -- the mod-7 resonances are exactly where Galois-equivariance should constrain the phase.",
