          "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
          "evidence": "I re-implemented the Z[zeta_7] arithmetic from scratch (basis 1..z^5, z^6=-(1+...+z^5); independent of the kps scripts) and re-derived every claimed fact from the D7 definition. ALL claims hold, AND the honest negative conclusion (no wide-E bound) is correct.\n\nSTRUCTURAL CLAIMS — CONFIRMED EXACT (04-computation/lrc14_qr_exact_struct_ec.py; 05-knowledge/results/lrc14_qr_exact_struct_ec.out):\n- Gauss sum g^2 = -7 exactly.\n- (2) Galois equivariance D7(a*c)=sigma_a(D7(c)): 276/276 (c,a) pairs hold EXACTLY (0 fails).\n- (3) Trace collapse: sum_{a in F7*} D7(ac) is rational on every test; Tr(D7(1,1,1,1,1,1)) = 5040 = 7! exactly.\n- (4) Reality: sigma_6 = complex conjugation and D7(6c)=conj(D7(c)) EXACTLY (0 fails) — since 6=-1 is a non-residue. The n<->-n lattice pairing therefore cancels imaginary parts exactly => correction RIGOROUSLY REAL.\n\nMAGNITUDE CLAIMS — CONFIRMED via full 6^6=46656 scan (04-computation/lrc14_qr_fastscan_ec.py; results/lrc14_qr_fastscan_ec.out): max imag(Tr)=2.7e-11 (Tr is rational), sum Tr over all cosets = 0, max|Tr| = 9240 = 2^3*3*5*7*11 (at c=(1,1,1,1,1,4)), and sum Tr vanishes on EACH #QR-pattern class (k=0..6 all 0). Orbit-rep version: 7776 dilation-orbit reps, sum Tr over reps = 0, max|Tr| = 9240. All match the claim.\n\nTHE GAP — CONFIRMED as a genuine obstruction, not a fixable gap (04-computation/lrc14_qr_lattice_gap_ec.py; results/lrc14_qr_lattice_gap_ec.out):\n- On real relation lattices (AP8 consec and WIDE8 odd-AP), Im/Re of the correction ~ 1e-14..1e-16 at all L=3,4,5: the n<->-n pairing makes the correction REAL — a usable lattice symmetry.\n- BUT the dilation c->ac is NOT a lattice symmetry: within-orbit lattice-weight spread GROWS with cutoff (AP8: 0.127, 0.638, 1.097 at L=3,4,5; WIDE8: 0.063, 0.370, 0.999), so Sum_c W_c D7(c) does NOT regroup into Sum_orbits W*Tr(D7).\n- The honest envelope sum|W| GROWS with L (AP8: 0.023->0.041->0.062; WIDE8: 0.012->0.022->0.033), confirming no finite magnitude bound from the trace.\n- Q(sqrt-7) check: only 4/404 sampled cosets have D7 fixed by sigma_2, so the QR/NQR index-2 split does NOT diagonalize — the full F_7^* trace is required, and the integer lattice does not realize it.\n\nVERDICT: The QR/Gauss-sum (Euler even-factor) angle delivers exactly what the claim states — a RIGOROUS REALITY reduction of the conditionally-convergent correction Sum K(n) (imaginary parts cancel exactly via n<->-n), via three exactly-verified structural identities (Galois-equivariance, integer field-trace collapse, sigma_6=conjugation). It does NOT yield a magnitude/convergence bound for wide E, because the trace collapse depends on the F_7^* dilation which is not a lattice symmetry. This is a REAL proof handle (the reality reduction is usable and exact) but NOT the wide-E bound the crux needs — the claim's own assessment is accurate. The conditionally-convergent signed/coset cancellation remains the open analytic content. Net: the angle is a confirmed-but-partial handle; it advances rigor (reality) but does not close the bound for wide E. Files: 04-computation/lrc14_qr_exact_struct_ec.py, lrc14_qr_fastscan_ec.py, lrc14_qr_lattice_gap_ec.py, lrc14_qr_adversarial_verify_ec.py (and matching .out files in 05-knowledge/results/)."
