          "evidence": "Independently re-verified with a fresh exact-Fraction meas_S7 implementation (different breakpoint sweep). The claim's NEGATIVE core and its rigorous handle are CONFIRMED; its POSITIVE residual (\"dyadic richness is the mechanism / exact tiebreaker\") is REFUTED by the cleanest causal test.\n\nCONFIRMED (all exact, reproduced to the digit):\n- consec{1..8} p_0 = 2447/5880 = 0.416156, UNIQUE global max 1/1287 at k=8. Also unique global max at k=9 (1/715) and k=10 (1/286) — extends claim's k=8,9 to k=10. No non-consec set ties or beats consec at k=8,9,10.\n- richness(C2)-max sets all have p_0 in [0.18128, 0.29252] (<=0.293).\n- Headline correlations: corr(p_0,contiguity/maxrun)=+0.2682, corr(p_0,C2)=+0.1562, corr(p_0,#distinct-odd)=-0.1895 (claimed +0.268/+0.156/-0.190).\n- Stratified richness corr by run: {6:+0.746, 7:+0.828, 8:+0.983}.\n- Doubling-monotonicity certificate: k=8 40/40, k=9 36/36 STRICT decreases. Stronger: consec{1..8} is a strict local max under ALL single-element replacements within {1..13} (40/40 decrease, 0 increase, 0 equal).\n\nREFUTED / OVERSTATED (the load-bearing caveat — dyadic richness is NOT the mechanism):\n- Decisive causal test (PART 3B/PART 6): removing chain-top 8 (BREAKS the 1-2-4-8 power-of-2 chain) costs only 0.014-0.081 in p_0; removing non-chain 5 (leaves a hole in {1..8}) costs 0.12-0.25. Avg p_0-drop removing a power-of-2 element = 0.151 < avg removing a non-chain element = 0.205. This INVERTS the dyadic-chain prediction: if the chain were load-bearing, breaking it should hurt most. It hurts least. The real driver is interval contiguity (gap-filling), not dyadic structure.\n- The \"windows ordered by power-of-2 chain length\" sub-claim is cherry-picked: holds for windows starting at 1,2,3 only. Across all six size-8 windows it MISPREDICTS — window {4..11} (pow2chain=2) has p_0=0.29569 < window {5..12} (pow2chain=1) p_0=0.30232. So pow2-chain is not a monotone predictor of p_0.\n\nGENUINE PROOF HANDLE (real, not a pretty analogy): consec{1..k} is the exact UNIQUE global maximizer of p_0 at every binding k (8,9,10), certified rigorously by exhaustion + a strict single-swap local-max property. The Glaisher/dyadic overlay is a correlational shadow of contiguity, not a causal mechanism or tiebreaker, and should not be relied on as a proof ingredient.\n\nSEPARATE OBSERVATION (not the verify target, but flagged): at k=8 consec p_0=0.41616 EXCEEDS cap_8=2243/5880=0.38146, and at k=9 p_0=0.50448 > cap_9=1979/4004=0.49426; only k=10 satisfies p_0=0.58146 <= cap_10=55/91=0.60440. If 'p_0(E)<=cap_k for all primitive E' is the route's closing requirement, the consec set violates it at k=8,9 as currently stated — worth reconciling with the binding-cluster framing.\n\nScripts (all exact, independent): C:\\Users\\Eliott\\Documents\\GitHub\\math\\04-computation\\lrc14_verify_glaisher_indep.py, lrc14_verify_glaisher_part2.py, lrc14_verify_glaisher_part3.py, lrc14_verify_glaisher_part4.py."
